          "source": "palm",
          "verdict": "malicious",
          "analysis": "The sample is a DDoS bot for the MIPS architecture, commonly found in IoT devices. The binary daemonizes itself using a double-fork mechanism in `main` and connects to a hardcoded command-and-control (C2) server. It receives commands to launch various flood attacks, which are handled in the `processCmd` function. These attacks include `UDPRAW`, `STD`, `OVH`, `RANDHEX`, and `XTD`, implemented in dedicated functions like `UDPRAW`, `SendSTD`, and `ovhl7`. The presence of explicit bot-related user-agent strings, such as `TheSuBot/0.2` and `www.billybobbot.com`, and its core functionality of launching network floods confirm its malicious nature.",
